-- title:
--   Formal quotient datum with coefficient and adic-point laws
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic filtration, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. Let $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicative) satisfy $vdet(g)=n$ iff $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $\Gamma\le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ scalar and $vdet(\sigma z)=2$ and an element $w$ with $vdet(\sigma w)=1$, let $\Gamma'$ consist of the $x\in\Gamma$ with $vdet(\sigma x)$ even, let $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ send $g$ to the class of $\sigma g$, and assume $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite vertex stabilisers and finitely many orbits on the lattice-homothety vertices of $\mathcal O$ in $K_0$; let $g_1=\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$. Then there is a formal quotient datum $D$ for these data — schemes $Y_n$ proper over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transition maps $yt_n$, and maps $q_n$ from pairs $(\psi,P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over a $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(B)\to Y_n$, compatible with base change, with $yt_n$ and with the twisted $\Gamma$-action — with two further properties. First (coefficient law), $q_n(\psi,P)=q_n(\psi',P)$ whenever $\psi$ and $\psi'$ agree on all $y$ with $\mathrm{Fr}(\mathrm{Fr}\,y)=y$. Second (adic-point law), for every complete algebraically closed valued field $C$ over $K_0$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ inside $C$ with a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi$ of $K_0$ in $C$ such that `IsAdicFrame` $\pi\,\varpi\,R$ holds (so $R$ is the unit ball of $C$, $\pi$-adically complete, $\mathcal O$ the unit ball of $K_0$, and $\pi\mapsto\varpi$), and every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_0:Onr\to R$: every family of maps $\mathrm{Spec}(R/\pi^{n+1})\to Y_n$ lying over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and compatible with the transitions $yt_n$ equals $\big(q_n(\psi_0\bmod\pi^{n+1},x_n)\big)_n$ for some adic point $x$ of $\hat\Omega$ over $R$, i.e. a compatible system of Deligne data over the $R/\pi^{n+1}$; and two adic points $x,x'$ have the same images under all $q_n$ if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` relating $(\psi_0\bmod\pi^{n+1},x_n)$ to $(\psi_0\bmod\pi^{n+1},x'_n)$ via $\sigma\gamma$ for every $n$, that is, the first components differ by the Frobenius twist by $-vdet(\sigma\gamma)$ and the Deligne data by pullback along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the existence of the formal quotient of Drinfeld's $p$-adic upper half plane by a discrete cocompact group in the form used on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side of the argument, with the two supplementary laws — dependence of the quotient map on the coefficient map only through the fixed ring of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$, and the identification of the inverse limit of the $R$-points of the tower with the $\Gamma$-orbits of adic points of $\hat\Omega$ — asserted alongside the datum, since neither follows from its defining fields. It feeds the statements on the behaviour of the Čerednik–Drinfeld map under change of coefficient map, on its adic-point description, and on the bare existence of a formal quotient datum.
